# GitHub workflow

- Repositories are **private** by default. Never create a public repo unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do all feature work on `feature/{feature-detail}` (lowercase, hyphens). Examples: `feature/slice-5-ui`, `feature/add-sim-picker`.
- Never commit directly to `main`. Open a pull request from the feature branch into `main`.
- PR title/body should summarize why; include a short test plan when behavior changes.
- After merge, continue from updated `main` (or the next `feature/...` branch).
